course: dictionary
lesson: 8669
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which meaning the writer means. Secretary is one of these words.
explain: In «Jake had been sent to the head teacher's office so often that the secretary just said "the usual chair, Jake?"», the words office, head teacher and sent are the clues. They show that the secretary is the person who helps in the school office, not a government minister.
explain: Always check by swapping your meaning into the sentence. "The office helper just said, the usual chair, Jake?" still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: A secretary is a person whose job is to help in an office, for example by typing letters, answering the phone and keeping records.
fact: The school secretary works in the school office and deals with visitors, absences, lunch money and phone calls.
fact: In government, a Secretary is the head of a department, such as the Home Secretary (UK) or the Secretary of State (USA).
fact: The secretary of a club writes down what happens at meetings.
fact: Phrases like «school secretary», «Home Secretary» and «club secretary» show you which meaning is being used.
exercise: In «Jake had been sent to the head teacher's office so often that the secretary just said "the usual chair, Jake?"», where does the secretary work? | On the football pitch | *In the school office | Inside a shop on the high street | At the top of a mountain
exercise: The club needs someone to write down what happens at each meeting. Which word fits best? | *secretary | referee | captain | teacher
exercise: A news lesson says, "The Home Secretary spoke to Parliament today." What kind of person is the Home Secretary? | A cleaner who works in the school | *A government minister who heads a department | A kind of school lunch | A player in the club team
test: Which phrase names a top government minister? | club secretary | school secretary | *Home Secretary | office chair
test: What is the best way to check the meaning of a word in context? | Look only at the first letter of the word | Guess the first meaning you think of and never check | Skip the sentence and forget it | *Swap your meaning into the sentence and see if it still makes sense
exam: Ella reads, "The secretary of the chess club kept all the records." What does secretary mean here? | A head of a government department | *A person who writes down and keeps records for a club | A machine for cooking | A teacher who teaches chess
